id: monster-form-violent-monster
name: Violent Monster
order: 2
slot: trait
# Its [Permanent] effects: they hold outside the Transformation too.
permanent: 1
# (1) "design a Super Signature Technique ... known as your 'Vile Technique'" - one of your Signature Techniques chosen, as Favored Technique's.
choose: ownTechnique
chosenTechnique: Vile Technique
# Free (the user's): no Technique Points of the character's on it, up to its 25 (technique.mjs signatureOf).
chosenTechniqueFreeTP: 25
description: >
  Your monstrous state leaves you prone to fits of rage, increasing your strength.
text: >
  Violent Monster: Your monstrous state leaves you prone to fits of rage, increasing your strength.
  (1)-[Permanent, Ruling]: Upon gaining access to this Transformation, design a Super Signature Technique with a TP Cost of up to 25. This Signature Technique is known as your 'Vile Technique'. You only have access to your Vile Technique while you are in Monster Form and have access to the Violent Monster Trait.
  (2)-[Passive]: Increase the Strike Rolls of your Attacking Maneuvers by 1(T) if all of the target(s) of that Attacking Maneuver are below a lower Health Threshold than you.
  (3)-[Passive]: Increase the Wound Rolls of your Attacking Maneuvers by 1(T) for each Health Threshold the target(s) are below. If there are multiple targets, this increase to Wound Rolls is based on the target above the highest Health Threshold.
  (4)-[Passive]: Double the bonus to your Wound Rolls for the 3rd effect of Violent Monster if the Attacking Maneuver is your Vile Technique.
  (5)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you or an Ally knock an Opponent through a Health Threshold with an Attacking Maneuver, you may use the Basic Attack Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver. If you do, you must target the Opponent knocked through a Health Threshold to trigger this effect with that Attacking Maneuver.
  (6)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you Defeat an Opponent or knock them through a Health Threshold with an Attacking Maneuver, regain Life and Ki Points equal to 1/2 of the Attribute Modifier for the Attribute you chose through the first effect of Monstrous Ascension.
  (7)-[Triggered, 1/Encounter]: If you use your Vile Technique, you may apply the Ascended Signature Advantage to that Attacking Maneuver.

---

# (1) The Vile Technique: one of your Signature Techniques, chosen as it is gained (as Favored Technique's) - changeable with its pencil; used
# only while in Monster Form with this Trait (technique-use.mjs). Designed on the Signature Techniques tab - a Super of 25 TP or less, free
# (its header); its level and its TP not checked here. (2) Strike against the lower, (5) the Basic Attack out of sequence: the table's.

# (3) Wound Rolls 1(T) for each Health Threshold the target is below.
[passive, effect 3]
wound.perTargetThreshold += 1(T);

# (4) Doubled on the Vile Technique: its 1(T) once more there (chat.mjs aggressionAgainst).
[passive, effect 4]
wound.perTargetThresholdChosen += 1(T);

# (7) Using the Vile Technique, once an Encounter: the Ascended Signature Advantage offered (use-maneuver.mjs).
[passive, effect 7]
allow chosenTechnique.ascend;

# (6) Defeating an Opponent or knocking one through a Health Threshold, once a Round: Life and Ki, half the chosen Attribute's Modifier.
[triggered/knock-through, 1/round, effect 6]
requires knockedOpponent;
if ($is.attribute.ag == 1) {
    life.value += floor(agility.mod / 2);
    ki.value += floor(agility.mod / 2);
}
if ($is.attribute.te == 1) {
    life.value += floor(tenacity.mod / 2);
    ki.value += floor(tenacity.mod / 2);
}
if ($is.attribute.fo-ma == 1) {
    life.value += floor(max(force.mod, magic.mod) / 2);
    ki.value += floor(max(force.mod, magic.mod) / 2);
}

[triggered/defeat-opponent, 1/round, effect 6]
if ($is.attribute.ag == 1) {
    life.value += floor(agility.mod / 2);
    ki.value += floor(agility.mod / 2);
}
if ($is.attribute.te == 1) {
    life.value += floor(tenacity.mod / 2);
    ki.value += floor(tenacity.mod / 2);
}
if ($is.attribute.fo-ma == 1) {
    life.value += floor(max(force.mod, magic.mod) / 2);
    ki.value += floor(max(force.mod, magic.mod) / 2);
}
